{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>For a month of days.</b> This is among the worthy — they are wasting away on their beds and afterward their souls depart; but of the wicked He says ״הַבָּשָׂר עוֹדֶנּוּ בֵּין שִׁנֵּיהֶם״ (verse 33). So is it taught in Sifrei, but in Mekhilta it is taught the opposite: the wicked eat and suffer for thirty days, and the worthy — the flesh is still between their teeth." "<b>Until it comes out of your nostrils.</b> As its Targum renders: ״דִּי תְּקוֹצוּן בֵּיהּ״ — it shall seem to you as though you have eaten of it in excess, until it exits and is repelled to the outside through the nostrils." "<b>And it shall be to you for a thing rejected.</b> That you will push it away more than you drew it near. And in the words of Rabbi Moshe the Darshan I saw that there is a term with which they call the sword זָרָא." "<b>Who is in your midst.</b> Had I not planted My Shekhinah among you, your heart would not have been lifted to enter into all these matters (Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:26.460504906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}